// GAP (isolated 2026-08-02, NOT fixed): the spawn race scan cannot see through
// a funcptr STRUCT FIELD. `worker` touches no global directly — only `o.cb()` —
// so the non-shared-global scan finds nothing, yet the child reaches `counter`
// through the callback while the parent writes it.
//
// The shape is NARROWER than first documented. Two nearby shapes ARE caught, and
// isolating this one required avoiding both:
//   * passing the struct by POINTER  -> caught by the non-shared-pointer rule
//   * reading the Ops struct from a GLOBAL -> caught by the global-access scan
// So the struct must pass BY VALUE and the worker must touch no global directly.
//
// Compile-clean today = the gap. Move to tests/zer_fail/ when fixed.
// See docs/limitations.md "spawn race scan blind to a funcptr STRUCT-FIELD call".
u32 counter;
void bump() { counter += 1; }
struct Ops { *() cb; }
void worker(Ops o) { o.cb(); }
u32 main() {
    Ops ops;
    ops.cb = bump;
    spawn worker(ops);
    counter += 1;
    return counter;
}
